      "source": "https://boston.wiki/a/Chinatown"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Boston's Chinatown was established in the 1870s and has been an Asian American cultural hub for over 150 years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bpl.org/blogs/post/researching-the-history-of-bostons-chinatown/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Chinese Progressive Association, founded in the 1970s, has championed workers' rights, affordable housing, and accountability for institutions bordering the neighborhood.",
